puts and original training, the mechanically wrong grouping gives the lowest changed-tool forecast loss among the six arms (1.26874 nats) but the highest original-tool loss (1.24071 nats). Correct grouping replacement gives a smaller changed-tool gain and original-tool penalty. Independent reconstruction, all 21,120 paired estimates and both complete replays verify this constructed-method reversal; prediction does not establish learned mechanics, historical process correspondence or human intent.","numerical_acceptance":true,"scope":"version report,FINDINGS,theory table AND summary,exchange,README/WALKTHROUGH,METHODS,status,coverage;publication separate"}
